Adapted the request-admission, cancellation and request-exit design in Rust,
using the existing Anima ModelAdapter transport. This is a narrow behavioral
port, not a copied Python runtime. Local changes: durable workspace-wide
reservations and attempt keys, default-off owner policy, bounded single-run
evidence, one no-tools generation, strict anchored advice, no evaluator or
canonical memory/skill writes, recovery without replay and versioned owner
decisions. The upstream full-history AIAgent fork and direct store-writing
tools are intentionally not imported. No private Hermes profiles are read.

